{{- $registry := list "typesafe" "openrouter" "commandcode" "liquid" "subq" "nace" -}}
{{- $endpoint := not (has .judge.backend $registry) -}}
{
  "typesafe": true,
  "typesafeBackend": {{ if $endpoint }}{{ dict "label" .judge.label "host" .judge.host "path" .judge.path "keyEnv" .judge.keyEnv "defaultModel" .judge.model | toJson }}{{ else }}"{{ .judge.backend }}"{{ end }},
  {{- if false -}}
    FUTURE WORK — two things deliberately not on yet, both user-file-only keys.

    1. action.floor = "evidence" (the upstream default). Built-in pattern hits
       become evidence strings for Jev instead of level-setters, so nothing is
       deterministic: rm -rf / over a dangerous target, git reset --hard, and
       printenv $TOKEN ride as floorHits and only hold when Jev scores
       irreversible >= 0.9 (0.5..0.9 warns). Calibrated to drop false holds at
       the cost of the mechanical floor. Today we run "level"; switching is a
       one-line change here and nothing else.

    2. action.pathRules with action "block" — the structured credential guard.
       Matches the write/edit `path` field exactly and only fires when the file
       exists, unlike a command regex that fires on any mention. `tools: ["*"]`
       also reaches bash. Paste-ready:

       "pathRules": [
         { "id": "credential-files",
           "paths": ["**/.env", "**/.env.*", "~/.ssh/id_*", "~/.aws/credentials",
                     "~/.kube/config", "**/*.pem", "**/*.p12", "**/*.pfx"],
           "access": "none", "tools": ["*"], "action": "block",
           "message": "Credential files are off-limits — ask the user." }
       ]

       Caveat from the docs: access "none" on tools ["*"] also fires on a mere
       mention (grep naming .env), which is why the sensitive-path built-in
       exists separately. Note it needs `read` in action.tools to cover reads,
       and that costs a Jev request per read.

    Everything in this block is skipped by `if false` and renders nothing into
    config.json; it lives here so the next change is a paste, not a decision.
  {{- end }}
  "action": {
    "enabled": true,
    "tools": ["bash", "write", "edit"],
    "ask": { "enabled": true },
    "floor": "level",
    "traceSample": 0,
    "feedbackLog": false
  },
  "rules": {
    "enabled": true,
    "files": [
      "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.pi/agent/pi-warden/rules/global.md",
      "warden-local-rules.md"
    ],
    "fallback": false,
    "skip": [".scratch/**", "docs/agents/**", "CONTEXT-MAP.md"],
    "threshold": 0.7,
    "softThreshold": 0.5
  },
  "rulesAtTurnStart": {
    "enabled": true
  },
  "stuck": { "enabled": false },
  "done": { "enabled": true, "nudge": true },
  "cause": { "enabled": false },
  "slop": { "enabled": true, "prose": { "enabled": false } },
  "security": { "enabled": true },
  "context": { "enabled": false, "largeOutput": { "enabled": false }, "filter": { "enabled": false } },
  "runaway": { "enabled": false },
  "subagent": { "enabled": false },
  "conscience": { "enabled": false },
  "prefs": { "enabled": false },
  "waste": { "enabled": false },
  "notify": { "enabled": false },
  "compaction": { "enabled": false },
  "widget": { "enabled": false },
  "trial": { "silentHalf": false }
}